Observations: My first regression check of the read-once pin was INVALID and I nearly shipped on it. I "reverted" to two reads but left the snapshot line in place, so there were three head -c calls instead of two, the forged bytes landed on the digest check instead of the verdict parse, and the suite passed — I read that as "the pin does not work". A faithful revert (snapshot removed) shows the pin failing exactly as intended, with the forged clean verdict marked and rc=0. Lesson: when a regression check says your new test is useless, suspect the reconstruction before the test. Fourth time this branch that something passed or failed for a reason other than the one it named.

